                <pb facs="0576" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/772: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-02T12:00:00+08:00">January 2,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 2—6:22 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. My 1206, December 31, 10 a.m. Following from American Consul at Harbin: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item><quote rend="blockquote"><p>“December 31, 10 a.m. Tsai and Soviet
                                    party arrived Harbin this morning from Changchun. They were met
                                    by a few Chinese but many Soviet adherents waving red flags.
                                    Local press reports that Mo Te-hui has been appointed <hi
                                        rendition="#italic">Tupan</hi> of Chinese Eastern
                                    Railway.”</p>
                            </quote></item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item><quote rend="blockquote"><p>“December 31, 4 p.m. Soviet prisoners,
                                    including those arrested at Soviet Consulate General May last,
                                    liberated today. Meeting of new board of directors of railway
                                    took place at 2 p.m. and new Soviet General Manager Rudy and
                                    Assistant Manager Denisoff took over chargé of administration of
                                    railway at 3:10 p.m. today.”</p>
                            </quote></item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
